# Shell scripts must survive a Windows checkout: a CRLF shebang script fails under
# Linux `sh` with "set: Illegal option -
", which is how the clean-room gate was
# found to be broken when run from the repository rather than a copy.
* text=auto
*.sh text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
LICENSE text eol=lf
NOTICE text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
# Compressed evidence must round-trip byte for byte: the test compares its SHA-256
# against the hash pinned at fetch time, and a line-ending rule would silently
# break that on checkout.
*.gz -text
# Hooks are run by git itself, which on a POSIX host execs the file directly:
# a CRLF shebang fails with `set: Illegal option -`, the same defect that
# broke the clean-room script. The executable bit is set in the index by
# `git update-index --chmod=+x`, not by this file.
tools/hooks/* text eol=lf
